<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Silvius I Nimrod, Duke of Württemberg-Oels</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1622–1664</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silvius">Silvius</a> I Nimrod (1622–1664) was a prince of the House of Württemberg who in 1647 married Elisabeth Marie, heiress of the last Poděbrady duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olesnica">Oleśnica</a>, and so became Duke of Oleśnica (Oels). He founded the Württemberg-Oels line, which ruled the Silesian duchy until it passed by marriage to the house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> in the 18th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/silvius-i-nimrod-duke-of-wurttemberg-oels.jpg" alt="Silvius I Nimrod, Duke of Württemberg-Oels" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silviuswuertt.-oels.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
